### Authentication Flow

```
1. POST /auth/register
   - Normalize username (lowercase, strip)
   - Validate password strength (min length + complexity)
   - Hash password with bcrypt
   - Write UserAccount to DB
   - Issue access token (30 min TTL) + refresh token (7 days TTL)
   - Access token claims: sub (user_id), workspace_id, role, scopes, token_version

2. POST /auth/login
   - Load user by username
   - Verify bcrypt hash
   - Issue new access + refresh tokens with current token_version

3. GET /protected-route
   - Extract Bearer token from Authorization header
   - Validate JWT signature, expiry, audience, issuer
   - Check required scopes (provenance:write provenance:read)
   - Enforce workspace scope on any record access

4. POST /auth/refresh
   - Validate refresh token
   - Load user from DB
   - Compare token_version claim to DB value — mismatch = revoked
   - Issue new access token

5. POST /auth/logout
   - Increment user.token_version in DB
   - All existing access + refresh tokens are now invalid
```

### Ingest Pipeline

```
POST /ingest or WS /ws/capture
         │
         ▼
  ingest_normalizer.py
  ├── Resolve workspace_id from payload or auth.workspace_id
  ├── Extract inserted_code, file_path, timestamp
  ├── Extract prompt_messages, model_name, raw_model_response
  ├── Warn if no client-provided UUID (retries will duplicate)
  └── Return NormalizedIngestPayload

         │
         ▼
  provenance_service.py
  ├── Infer language from file extension
  ├── ast_normalizer.py → AST node-type sequence
  ├── embedding_service.py → 256-dim vector
  ├── Write ProvenanceRecord to PostgreSQL
  ├── If Neo4j enabled: create AIGeneratedBlock + ProvenanceBlockVersion
  ├── Save lineage_node_id back to Postgres record
  ├── Commit (on failure: cleanup Neo4j node if created)
  └── Return record UUID
```

### Middleware Stack

Applied outermost first:

1. `TrustedHostMiddleware` — if `BACKEND_TRUSTED_HOSTS` is set
2. `CORSMiddleware` — explicit origins, no wildcard in production
3. `apply_security_headers` — X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy, COOP, CORP, Permissions-Policy, HSTS (production only)
4. `enforce_http_payload_size` — streaming body read, 2 MB default limit
5. `enforce_http_rate_limit` — in-memory sliding window, 120 req/60 s default, exempt `/health`

