## SECTION 9: PRODUCT POSITIONING

### What Makes LineageLens Unique

No other tool tracks the provenance of AI-generated code. Tools exist that review code for bugs, security issues, or style. None answer:

**"This function was written by an AI — which one, in response to what prompt, with what model, and what risk signals did the generated code contain at insertion time?"**

LineageLens is the first system that captures provenance at insertion time, stores it persistently, and surfaces it at review time.

### Differentiation from Traditional Debugging Tools

| Traditional Debugging | LineageLens |
|---|---|
| Looks at what code does | Looks at where code came from |
| Operates at runtime or static analysis | Operates at write time |
| Knows the author is a human | Knows which AI tool wrote it |
| Requires a bug to exist | Captures context before a bug appears |
| No concept of "prompt" | Stores the prompt that produced the code |
| No model provenance | Tracks model name, version, parameters, session |

### Key Value Propositions

**For developers:** When something goes wrong in AI-generated code, know exactly what was asked, what the model produced, and what the surrounding context was — without reconstructing it from memory.

**For engineering leads:** See your team's AI coding patterns: which models, which files, how much, what risk level — across all developers in the workspace.

**For compliance/security teams:** AI-generated code is in your codebase. LineageLens gives you the audit trail to prove what was generated, when, by which model, and whether it contained sensitive patterns at insertion time.

