## SECTION 10: BUSINESS MODEL

**Base** — Free or low one-time price
- Single user, self-hosted Docker
- Capture + explain only
- No team features, no semantic search
- Target: individual engineers experimenting with AI tools

**Plus** — Monthly subscription per workspace
- 5–50 developers
- Full feature set: capture, semantic search, governance dashboard, team management
- Self-hosted Docker (customer's infrastructure)
- Target: engineering teams at product companies, agencies, startups

**Max** — Annual contract
- Unlimited users, multi-workspace support
- Neo4j graph lineage + all Plus features
- Priority support, SLA, audit export
- Managed hosting available as add-on
- Target: regulated industries (fintech, healthcare), large engineering organizations with AI governance requirements

### Why Self-Hosted

Provenance records contain actual prompts and actual generated code — potentially including business logic, security code, and proprietary algorithms. Self-hosted deployment eliminates data-sensitivity objections: nothing leaves the customer's infrastructure. It also means zero infrastructure cost for the vendor in the primary distribution model.

### Why Subscription Works

Provenance is not a one-time problem. Teams writing AI-assisted code need ongoing capture and retention. The value compounds: the older the provenance record store, the more useful it is for audit, debugging, and governance. Teams do not churn from a tool that holds months of their AI coding history.

